## Final Judgement
### Step 1: Summarize Key Insights
The retrieved evidence shows that Hunter Biden served as the board chairman of the World Food Program USA (WFP USA), with records indicating he held this role around April 2016. However, the Nobel Peace Prize in 2020 was awarded to the United Nations World Food Programme (WFP). The evidence establishes that WFP USA is a separate, independent U.S.-based nonprofit organization and is legally distinct from the UN World Food Programme. Additionally, by late 2019, Randy Russell was serving as the board chairman of WFP USA. Because the evidence clearly distinguishes between the two organizations and clarifies Hunter Biden's specific role, no further investigation is required.

### Step 3: Conclusion
Based on the recorded evidence, the claim that Hunter Biden was the chairman of the Nobel Peace Prize-winning World Food Program is `refuted`. Although Hunter Biden was the board chairman of the World Food Program USA, this organization is a separate, independent legal entity from the United Nations World Food Programme, which is the actual recipient of the 2020 Nobel Peace Prize. Hunter Biden never served as the chairman of the Nobel-winning UN agency itself.

### Verdict: REFUTED

### Justification
The claim is refuted because Hunter Biden never served as the chairman of the United Nations World Food Programme, which won the Nobel Peace Prize in 2020 ([PBS NewsHour](https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/world-food-program-wins-nobel-peace-prize)). While Biden did serve as the board chairman of the World Food Program USA around April 2016 ([San Antonio Report](https://sanantonioreport.org/before-hunter-biden-there-was-billy-carter-neil-bush-and-others/world-food-program-usas-annual-mcgovern-dole-leadership-award-ceremony/)), this organization is a separate, independent U.S.-based nonprofit that is legally distinct from the UN agency ([Changing the Present](https://changingthepresent.org/collections/friends-of-the-world-food-program-inc)). Additionally, by late 2019, Randy Russell had assumed the role of board chairman for the World Food Program USA ([PR Newswire](https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/wfp-usa-names-unicef-usa-exec-as-new-president-and-ceo-300959962.html)).